# Utilities slice 5 — a Power bill, a tariff raised, and a brownout that bills nothing.
#
#   godot --path src/Borough.Godot -- --load plans/evidence/utilities-slice-5/ridge.borough \
#     --drive plans/evidence/utilities-slice-5/billing.drive
#
# The saved city opens on Day 2, fully delivered. Building 37 is the occupied dwelling in the east
# District; its Households run its lighting Rule and pay the Power tariff (Policy 0, power_tariff,
# 1 money per unit in powered.toml). Tiles are in ridge.geometry.txt.
#
# ⚠ ONE `shoot` PER TICK. The picture is taken on the next frame, so a second `shoot` on the same
# Tick throws the first away.
4097 pause
4097 overlay utilities
4097 ui building 37
4097 ui section utilities on
4097 tilt 45
4097 focus 225 3 90
4097 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-5/01-day1-bill.png
4097 speed 8

# The player raises the tariff from 1 to 4 per unit. It bills from the next firing.
4099 pause
4099 ui govern 0 4
4099 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-5/02-tariff-raised.png
4099 speed 8

# The crossing Street goes. Day 2 was settled whole at Tick 4,096, so Day 2 runs lit and is billed
# at 4; Day 3, settled at Tick 6,144, runs at nothing delivered.
4101 pause
4101 tilt 40
4101 focus 128 2 560
4101 hold street
4101 click 191 0 shift
4101 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-5/03-street-removed.png
4101 speed 8

# Day 3. The panel reports Day 2's bill at the raised tariff.
6150 pause
6150 hold look
6150 ui building 37
6150 tilt 45
6150 focus 225 3 90
6150 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-5/04-day2-bill-raised.png
6150 speed 8
6152 pause
6152 ui budget on
6152 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-5/05-budget.png
6152 speed 8

# Day 4. Day 3 ran browned out, so it billed what the dwelling received.
8200 pause
8200 ui budget off
8200 ui building 37
8200 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-5/06-day3-brownout-bill.png
8200 quit
